    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256">

                <pb facs="0617" n="589" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v01/pg589"/>

                <head>256. Telegram From the Embassy in Vietnam to the
                        Department of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d256-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Saigon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1964-08-02T21:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2,
                                1964—9 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>281. CINCPAC for POLAD. Ref <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Maddox</hi> incident, most important that we be
                    authorized to give facts to GVN before Hanoi
                    breaks story and falsified version is disseminated. Request official version to
                    be used and, when determined, what action USG
                    expects to take. Please indicate how much of this latter information can be
                    passed to GVN.</p>
                <p>As you are aware, operational radio traffic relating to this incident was in
                    clear.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Taylor</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d256-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d256-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Vietnam Working Group Files: Lot 72 D 219, DeSoto
                    Patrols, August. Confidential; Flash. Repeated to CINCPAC. Received at 8:46
                    a.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
